msgid "They celebrate the year passing same time each year. Each time, I put a notch in the beam there."
msgstr "彼らは毎年同じ時期に年の経過を祝うの。そのたびに、私はあそこの梁に切り込みを一つ入れるの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The woman pointed at a wooden beam near the door. It had twenty-some notches."
msgstr "その女はドアの近くにある木製の梁を指さした。そこには二十数個の切り込みがあった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah felt her stomach drop."
msgstr "サラは胃が落ちるのを感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made peace, as far she could, with her condition."
msgstr "彼女は、できる限り、自分の状況と折り合いをつけていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had made peace because in her heart she knew this was but a moment in her life. There would be a next phase to her life, she just knew it..."
msgstr "彼女はこれまで、これが人生の一時的な出来事に過ぎないと心の中で分かっていたからこそ、なんとか折り合いをつけてきたのだ。しかし、人生には次の段階があるはずだと、彼女は確信していた…"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "For the first time it dawned on Sarah that this might be her life. Forever."
msgstr "初めてサラは、これが自分の人生になるかもしれないと悟った。永遠に。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Twenty years? And nobody ever came for you?"
msgstr "20年？それで誰もあなたを探しに来なかったの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The woman shrugged again, still carrying on her work."
msgstr "その女性は再び肩をすくめ、作業を続けた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "The king wasn't gonna send any soldiers out into the desert to save some peasant girl, and the rest of my village was either dead or here with me."
msgstr "王は砂漠へ農民の娘を救うために兵士など送るつもりはなかったし、村の他の人々は死んだか、私と一緒にここにいるかのどちらかだったのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "So who was gonna save me?"
msgstr "じゃあ、誰が私を助けてくれるっていうの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah swallowed. She had no answer for the woman."
msgstr "サラは言葉を飲み込んだ。彼女にはその女性に返す言葉もなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It made her feel uneasy, realizing that this woman's fate as a slave had likely barely been more than an incidental report that her father had once read and dismissed."
msgstr "この女性が奴隷となった運命が、父親にとってかつて読み流しただけの付随的な報告に過ぎなかったかもしれないと気づいたことで、彼女は不安を感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "But you...you're from Rosanna too?"
msgstr "でも…あなたもロザンナ出身なの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Yeah..."
msgstr "ええ…"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Lots of our kind showing up around here lately."
msgstr "最近、私たちの種族がここによく見られるようになったのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Used to be most slaves came from the far east, but now you see our kind by the bundle, dragged around the markets."
msgstr "昔は奴隷のほとんどが極東から来ていたけど、今では市場で私たちの種族が束になって引きずられているのを見かけるようになったのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "I don't get much news around here, you know what's up? That bastard king still alive?"
msgstr "ここではあまりニュースを聞かないから、何が起きているか知ってる？あのクソ野郎の王様、まだ生きてるの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It pained Sarah to hear her talk about her father like that, but given her circumstance, she could hardly blame her."
msgstr "サラは、彼女が父親についてそのように話すのを聞いて心を痛めたが、彼女の置かれた状況を考えれば、彼女を責めることはほとんどできなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "No, the king died. The capital fell to the tribesmen."
msgstr "いいえ、王は死んだわ。首都は部族民に陥落したの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "That explains why we got so many of our kind showing up here, I guess."
msgstr "それで、我々のような者がなぜこんなに大勢ここに来たのか、説明がつくわね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It doesn't make you sad to hear your country fell?"
msgstr "故国が滅びたのを聞いて、悲しくないの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "My country? My country ain't never give a damn about me, so tell me why I should give a damn about it?"
msgstr "「私の国？ 私の国なんて、私のことなど気にも留めたことないんだ。じゃあ、なんで私が国のことなんか気にかける必要があるっていうの？」"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Ain't nobody else on this world but yourself. Best you focus on that."
msgstr "この世にはお前自身以外、誰もいないんだ。それだけに集中した方がいい。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The woman put down her kitchen tools and turned to Sarah."
msgstr "その女性は台所の道具を置き、サラの方を向いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Speaking of that..."
msgstr "そういえば……"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "I'd want to ask you if he didn't go too hard on you, but knowing him, he probably fucked you till your body gave out, right?"
msgstr "彼があなたをあまりにも激しく扱わなかったか聞きたいところだけど、彼の性格からして、きっと体が限界を迎えるまで犯し続けたんだろう？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah looked away, embarassed, but nodded."
msgstr "サラは恥ずかしそうに顔をそむけたが、頷いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Yeah...don't expect that to change any time soon."
msgstr "ええ…それがすぐに変わるなんて期待しないで。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "It's been twenty years and he still fucks me hard as the first time. Less often though, so it gets better."
msgstr "もう20年も経つのに、彼は今でも初夜と同じくらい激しく私を犯すの。ただ、頻度は減ったから、その分マシにはなったけど。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "The gods blessed that old bastard with an impossible luck and a cock that never stops, and he's used both to no end."
msgstr "神々はその老いぼれに信じられないほどの幸運と、決して止まらないペニスを授けた。そして彼はその両方を存分に利用してきたのだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She tossed a towel aside."
msgstr "彼女はタオルを脇に放り投げた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Terrible with money though, so I hope you're not used to livin in luxury, cause he ain't givin you none."
msgstr "金銭感覚は最悪だからね。だから、あなたが贅沢な暮らしに慣れてないことを願うわ。だって、彼はあなたにそんなもの一切与えてないんだから。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Terrible with money?"
msgstr "金遣いがひどいって？"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Yeah, take you for example. He was supposed to buy this month's food from the market, instead he comes back with you."
msgstr "ええ、例えばあなたのことを見てみましょう。彼は今月の食料を市場で買うはずだったのに、代わりにあなたを連れて帰ってきたんです。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah thought to herself it that was all she was worth now, a month's worth of food from a market."
msgstr "サラは心の中で思った。これが今や自分の価値のすべてなのか——市場で手に入る一ヶ月分の食料ほどの価値しかないと。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Buying another slave, he can barely maintain me..."
msgstr "別の奴隷を買うなんて、彼は私を養うことさえままならないのに…"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah could see the woman grow frustrated again."
msgstr "サラは、その女性が再び苛立っているのを見て取れた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Is that why you were angry yesterday?"
msgstr "昨日怒っていたのは、そのせいだったの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She nodded."
msgstr "彼女は頷いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "He only thinks with his fucking dick, and we get to suffer the consequences."
msgstr "彼はクソったれなチンコでしか考えてないのに、そのツケを払わされるのは私たちなのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Why did he buy me then?"
msgstr "じゃあ、なんで彼は私を買ってくれたの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She laughed as if the question itself had been absurd."
msgstr "彼女は、その質問自体が馬鹿げているかのように笑った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Look at yourself."
msgstr "自分を見てみなさい。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Tight, fit, and twenty years younger than me. Why you think he bought you?"
msgstr "引き締まってて、ぴったりしてて、私より20歳も若いんだから。彼がなんであなたを買ったと思うの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah felt herself grow red."
msgstr "サラは自分が顔を赤らめるのを感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The older woman walked across the room towards her and took her hands."
msgstr "年配の女性は部屋を横切って彼女の方へ歩み寄り、その両手を取った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Look, it ain't all bad."
msgstr "ほら、全部が悪いわけじゃないのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Tons of tribesmen out here violent as can be. He's rough, but he don't hit you or nothing. Not unless you give him reason to."
msgstr "「ここの多くの者たちと比べれば、彼に慣れれば、人生もそんなに悪くないってわかるようになるわ。」"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Once you get used to him, you'll learn life ain't that bad, compared to most others here."
msgstr "彼に慣れれば、ここの他のほとんどの人々と比べれば、人生もそれほど悪くないってわかるようになるわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She squeezed Sarah's hands."
msgstr "彼女はサラの手を握りしめた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Hell, it might even be nice to have a helper around the house. You look like you can work a kitchen, with some training, maybe."
msgstr "ちくしょう、家に手伝いがいるのも、案外悪くないかもしれないわね。少し訓練すれば、あなたも厨房で働けそうだし。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Kitchen work, this was what she had to look forward to when she wasn't in his bed being ravaged."
msgstr "厨房の仕事――彼とのベッドで激しく愛撫されていない時、彼女が期待できるのはこれだけだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Regardless, for now, Sarah knew she had few other options. She didn't even so much as know the layout of her street, let alone the entire city."
msgstr "いずれにせよ、今のところサラには他に選択肢がほとんどないことを彼女は理解していた。自分の家の街の配置すら知らないのに、街全体など知る由もなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Escaping right now, with so little information, might as well be suicide."
msgstr "今すぐ、これほど少ない情報で逃げ出すのは、自殺行為に等しいだろう。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah didn't know much about her situation, but she did know she wanted to live."
msgstr "サラは自分の状況について多くを知らなかったが、生きたいという願いだけははっきりしていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "If that meant putting up with this, she would."
msgstr "もしそれがこの状況に耐えることを意味するなら、彼女はそうするつもりだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Here, take these and chop up some of these vegetables."
msgstr "ほら、これを持って行って、これらの野菜をいくつか刻んで。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah joined Mary in the kitchen and began taking on tasks."
msgstr "サラはマリーと一緒に厨房に入り、作業に取り掛かり始めた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hadn't worked in a kitchen for a day in her life, but Sarah caught on fast enough."
msgstr "彼女はこれまで一日も厨房で働いたことがなかったが、サラはすぐにコツを掴んだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "As Mary showed her the ropes, she told Sarah more of her life."
msgstr "マリーが手ほどきをしている間、彼女はサラに自分の人生についてさらに詳しく語った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Listening to her tell her story, Sarah felt equal measure sympathy and fear."
msgstr "彼女の物語を聞きながら、サラは同情と恐怖を同じくらい感じていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sympathy for the woman's circumstance, how life had unfolded for her. Fear because in so many ways, she represented what Sarah wanted to avoid."
msgstr "彼女の境遇に同情を覚える。人生が彼女にとってどのように展開してきたのか。そして、彼女が多くの点でサラが避けたいと願っていた存在を体現していたことに、恐怖を感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Still, there was an easy flow to the kitchen work. It had a way of making Sarah forget, if only for a moment, where she was."
msgstr "それでも、台所の仕事には自然な流れがあった。その流れは、サラに、ほんの一時でも自分がどこにいるのかを忘れさせるようだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She was grateful for that."
msgstr "彼女はそれに感謝していた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a few hours later then the old soldier finally emerged from his bedroom and lazily walked into the kitchen."
msgstr "数時間後、その老いた兵士はようやく寝室から出てきて、気だるげに台所へと歩いていった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "As he walked into the kitchen, he casually smacked Sarah on her rear, causing her to let out a surprised shriek."
msgstr "彼が厨房に入ってくると、彼はサラの尻を気ままに叩き、彼女は驚きの声を上げた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "This only seemed to entertain him."
msgstr "それは彼をただ楽しませているようにしか見えなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "He walked over to Mary, seized her, and kissed her deeply."
msgstr "彼はマリーの方へ歩み寄り、彼女を掴んで深くキスをした。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Mary entertained it for a moment, before pushing him away. She was clearly more comfortable with resisting him."
msgstr "マリーはしばらく彼を楽しませていたが、やがて彼を突き放した。彼女が彼に抵抗することに明らかに心地よさを感じていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The old man spoke some words which seemed to agitate Mary."
msgstr "老人は、マリーを動揺させるような言葉をいくつか口にした。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Their voices rose, bordering on yelling, before the old soldier walked away, seemingly tired of the fight."
msgstr "二人の声は叫びに近いほど高まり、老いた兵士が口論に疲れたように立ち去る前に、その声は最高潮に達していた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "What was that about?"
msgstr "それは何のことだったの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Mary spoke their language. It would help Sarah get a better understanding of her situation."
msgstr "マリーは彼らの言語を話していた。それはサラが自分の状況をより深く理解する助けになるだろう。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "It's...I didn't want him to do that."
msgstr "それは…彼にそんなことをしてほしくなかったの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Yob'Gelah."
msgstr "ヤブゲラ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah didn't understand a word of it."
msgstr "サラはそれを一言も理解できなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "What does that mean?"
msgstr "それはどういう意味？"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "It...it means unity...or, well not quite, maybe it better translates as something like, merging into the family."
msgstr "それは…それは統一を意味するの…いや、正確には違うわね。たぶん、家族に溶け込む、といった感じの方がしっくりくるかしら。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It sounded harmless enough."
msgstr "それは、それほど無害に聞こえた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "He wants me to join...his family?"
msgstr "彼は私に…彼の家族に加わるように求めているの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Mary shook her head."
msgstr "マリーは首を横に振った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "That's what it means literally...but...it's more of a ritual."
msgstr "文字通りの意味ではそうだけど…でも、それって一種の儀式みたいなものなの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "a ritual?"
msgstr "儀式だって？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Mary looked around to see if the old soldier was out of sight, then she turned around and pulled up her skirt, revealing her lower back."
msgstr "マリーは老いた兵士が視界から消えたか確認するために周りを見渡し、それから振り返ってスカートをまくり上げ、腰の下部を露わにした。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Etched into her lower back, right above her rear, was a complicated symbol in deep black ink."
msgstr "彼女の腰の下部、ちょうど尻のすぐ上に、複雑な記号が深い黒インクで刻まれていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She dropped her skirt back down."
msgstr "彼女はスカートを再び下ろした。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "It's a family sigil."
msgstr "これは一族の紋章なの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "He's going to carry out the ritual with you..."
msgstr "彼はあなたと一緒に儀式を行うつもりなの…"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah felt her throat seize up."
msgstr "サラは喉が締め付けられるのを感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "I told him it didn't have to be done, but he insists."
msgstr "私は彼に、やらなくてもいいと伝えたのに、彼はそれでもやり通すつもりだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You...mean he's going to mark me? With that?"
msgstr "あなた…つまり、彼が私に印をつけるってこと？それで？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Mary nodded."
msgstr "マリーは頷いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "He asked me to buy the ink and the needles, so I knew right away what he was planning."
msgstr "彼は私にインクと針を買うように言ったから、彼が何を計画しているのかすぐにわかったの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "I tried to talk him out of it but I don't think he'll change his mind."
msgstr "彼を説得しようとしたけど、彼が考えを変えるとは思えないわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah felt her body shake."
msgstr "サラは体が震えるのを感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "To be this man's slave was one thing. That was a state of being that could change."
msgstr "この男の奴隷になること自体は一つのことだった。それは変化する可能性のある状態だったのだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But to carry on her body an indelible mark, showing her to be his property forever..."
msgstr "しかし、彼女の体に消えない印を刻み込み、彼女が永遠に彼の所有物であることを示すことまで…"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Please...can you ask him again?"
msgstr "お願い…彼にもう一度頼んでくれない？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Mary shrugged."
msgstr "マリーは肩をすくめた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Once he makes up his mind, it's not easy to get him to change."
msgstr "一度彼が決心してしまえば、考えを変えさせるのは簡単ではないの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "I can stretch it out for a few days. Tell him that the market is out of ink, but he'll only believe that for so long..."
msgstr "数日間は時間を稼げるわ。市場にインクがなくなったと伝えてみて。でも、彼がそれを信じてくれるのも、せいぜいしばらくだけだけど…"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "So what can I do?"
msgstr "じゃあ、私に何ができるっていうの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Just...keep your head down, for now, alright?"
msgstr "とりあえず…今は目立たないようにしてて、わかった？"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "I'll see if I can come up with something."
msgstr "何とか方法を考えてみるわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah nodded and resumed her kitchen work."
msgstr "サラは頷き、台所の作業を再開した。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She began to work harder and harder, hoping that the work would keep her from thinking about the ritual. It worked, partly."
msgstr "彼女はますます熱心に作業に取り組み始めた。仕事によって儀式のことを考えないようにと願ってのことだった。そして、それは部分的に効果があった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Time passes as Sarah poured herself into her work, until she could hear yelling from the other room."
msgstr "サラが仕事に没頭しているうちに、時間が経ち、やがて別の部屋から叫び声が聞こえてきた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah looked towards Mary."
msgstr "サラはマリーの方を見た。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "What is he saying?"
msgstr "彼は何と言っているの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Mary put down her knives and washed her hands."
msgstr "マリーはナイフを置き、手を洗った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Mary"
msgid "Don't worry, he wants me to come see him."
msgstr "心配しないで。彼は私に会いに来てほしいのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "With little more than that, Mary left to the other room."
msgstr "それだけ言うと、マリーは別の部屋へと去っていった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah tried to continue her work, but the sudden stillness of the house felt odd."
msgstr "サラは作業を続けようとしたが、家が急に静まり返ったことに違和感を覚えた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "As she was chopping another set of vegetables, the silence was softly broken by muted sounds from the next room."
msgstr "野菜をさらに刻んでいると、隣室から聞こえるかすかな物音によって静寂がそっと破られた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah put down her knife and listened intently."
msgstr "サラは包丁を置き、注意深く耳を澄ませた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
