msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Just finish them here. Use my desk."
msgstr "ここで終わらせて。私の机を使って。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Your...desk?"
msgstr "あなたの…机？"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Why not. Better to work on a proper desk than some improvised boxes, right?"
msgstr "いいじゃない。何もない箱で作業するより、ちゃんとした机でやった方がいいでしょ？"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Yeah but..."
msgstr "ええ、でも…"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "It's just...my Father he had a desk and one time when I used it, he got really angry and he..."
msgstr "ただ…父は机を持っていたの。一度私がそれを使った時、父はすごく怒って…"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah touched Samayra on the shoulder to calm her down."
msgstr "サラはサマヤラの肩に触れて彼女を落ち着かせようとした。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Hey, it's just you and me. And it's my desk, and I'm telling you it's fine, okay?"
msgstr "ねえ、いるのは私たち二人だけだろ。それに、これは私の机だし、大丈夫だって言ってるんだ、わかった？"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Okay..."
msgstr "わかったわ…"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Still somewhat hesitant, the girl took her seat behind the desk."
msgstr "まだいくらかためらいがちだったが、少女は机の後ろに腰掛けた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Whatever restraint she had quickly faded as she got into the work, her hands and the quill flowing like water."
msgstr "彼女が抱えていたどんな自制心も、仕事に取り掛かるやいなや消え去り、その手と羽根ペンはまるで水のように流れるように動いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "What?"
msgstr "何？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra didn't even look up as she kept working."
msgstr "サマヤラは作業を続けながら、顔も上げなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It's just impressive to see you working. You're so...productive."
msgstr "あなたが作業しているのを見るのは本当に感心するわ。本当に…生産的ね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra softly smiled."
msgstr "サマヤラは静かに微笑んだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Focus. Dedication. And good penmanship."
msgstr "集中力。熱意。そして、美しい字。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah watched Samayra's handwriting, beautiful."
msgstr "サラはサマヤラの美しい字を眺めていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Yeah, you're a lot better at it than me, that's for sure."
msgstr "ええ、あなたは私よりずっと上手ね。それは確かだわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Did you never have a teacher?"
msgstr "先生なんていなかったの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I did, and trust me, they beat my hands until they were purple, trying to make me write like a proper lady."
msgstr "教わったことはあるわ。でも信じて、彼らは私をまともな淑女のように書かせようと、手が紫色になるまで殴ったのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It still didn't stick."
msgstr "それでも、身につかなかったの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "In the end my dad just accepted that this was as good as I was ever going to get."
msgstr "結局のところ、父はこれが私がこれ以上上達できる限界だと受け入れたの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Yeah, I wasn't much good at most things, so I made up for it with stuff like this. This and dancing, mostly."
msgstr "ええ、私は大抵のことではあまり得意じゃなかったから、その分、こういうことや、主にダンスで補っていたの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah smiled, recalling memories of her own youth."
msgstr "サラは微笑み、自身の幼少期の記憶を思い出した。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Yeah, I was like that too."
msgstr "ええ、私も昔はそうだったわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Dancing, singing. On the whole, I don't think I was too bad."
msgstr "ダンスや歌など、全体的に見れば、私はそれほど悪くなかったと思うわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Was your dad proud of you?"
msgstr "お父さんはあなたのことを誇りに思っていましたか？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah was surprised by how stunned she felt at the question."
msgstr "サラは、その質問に自分がどれほど驚き、呆然としたかに気づいて驚いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I think so..."
msgstr "そう思うわ…"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "He told me he was...often. But I still wonder sometimes how much of it he meant, you know?"
msgstr "彼は私に、そう…よく言っていたわ。でも、時々今でも思うの。その言葉に、どれほどの本気があったのかって。わかる？"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "I get it. It can be hard, practicing all your life for something. For a role that was decided for you before you were even born."
msgstr "わかるよ。一生をかけて何かのために練習していくのは、難しいことかもしれない。生まれる前から決められていた役割のためにね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "And then I look at how my life turned out...I don't know what he'd think of it."
msgstr "そして、自分の人生がどうなったかを見てみると…父がそれをどう思うだろう、私には分からないの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra looked up."
msgstr "サマヤラは顔を上げた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "You're re-taking your country. He'd be proud, I'm sure of it."
msgstr "あなたは国を取り戻そうとしているのね。彼はきっと誇りに思うはずよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But I failed my brother...his son...Thomas."
msgstr "でも、私は弟を…彼の息子であるトマスを、見殺しにしてしまった…"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah heard her own voice slowly fade."
msgstr "サラは自分の声がゆっくりと消えていくのを感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra looked up from the desk."
msgstr "サマヤラは机から顔を上げた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Don't say that."
msgstr "そんなこと言わないで。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But it's true."
msgstr "でも、本当なの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "It's not true."
msgstr "本当じゃないわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "You always..."
msgstr "あなたはいつも…"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The girl sighed in a rare show of frustration."
msgstr "少女は珍しく苛立ちを見せ、ため息をついた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "You always take on all the troubles of the world and blame yourself for them."
msgstr "あなたはいつも、世界のすべての悩みを抱え込み、その責任を自分に負わせているのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "But you didn't know when you left Rosanna that that would happen. You had no way of knowing."
msgstr "でも、ロザンナを置いてきた時、そんなことになるなんて知らなかったでしょう。知る方法なんてなかったんだから。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "No, but-"
msgstr "いや、でも—"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Not but!"
msgstr "違うの！"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "You came to Bagrad and you saved me."
msgstr "バグラッドに来て、私を救ってくれたのね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "A nobody. You risked your life, facing down a demon, just to save me, a girl that meant nothing to you."
msgstr "取るに足らない存在だったのに。あなたは悪魔に立ち向かい、命を懸けて、あなたにとって何の意味もなかった少女である私を救ったのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "That's who you are, Sarah."
msgstr "それこそが、あなたの真の姿よ、サラ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "And if you had the chance, you would have saved Thomas, but...life doesn't work like that."
msgstr "もし機会があれば、君はトマスも救っただろう。でも…人生はそううまくいかないものだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Sometimes, things are just beyond our ability to change."
msgstr "時には、物事は我々の力で変えることのできない範囲にあることもある。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "And that doesn't mean it doesn't hurt, or that we can't be sad about it, but it does mean we can't punish ourselves for it."
msgstr "でも、だからといって、それが痛くないとか、悲しんではいけないということではない。ただ、そのことで自分を罰してはならないということだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Not all the time, at least."
msgstr "少なくとも、いつもそうとは限らない。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "You...you loved Thomas, I know that from each time you spoke about it. I see it in your face now."
msgstr "あなたは…あなたはトマスを愛していたのね。あなたが彼について話すたびに、私はそれを感じ取っていたわ。今もあなたの顔からそれがわかる。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "You would move the heavens if it would get him back."
msgstr "彼を取り戻すためなら、あなたは天さえも動かすでしょう。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "But...you're just a person, Sarah. An incredible person, but still just human."
msgstr "でも…サラ、あなたもただの人間じゃない。信じられないほど素晴らしい人間だけど、それでも結局は人間なのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah softly smiled as a tear ran down her face."
msgstr "サラは静かに微笑み、涙が頬を伝った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you, Samayra, for saying that."
msgstr "ありがとう、サマヤラ、そう言ってくれて。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Yeah..."
msgstr "ええ…"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well, I don't like to yell, but I'll keep yelling at you until one day you might actually believe me."
msgstr "まあ、叫ぶのは好きじゃないけど、いつかあなたが本当に信じてくれるまで、叫び続けるつもりよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Thank you for that too."
msgstr "それもありがとう。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Together they worked deep into the night."
msgstr "二人は夜が更けるまで共に作業を続けた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "In the end, Sarah fell asleep in her bed to the soft scratching sound of the quill running across the paper."
msgstr "結局、サラはベッドで眠りについた。ペンの紙を走る柔らかな音が、彼女の眠りを誘っていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She drifted into deep sleep as the girl carried on the work for the both of them."
msgstr "少女が二人分の作業を続けている間、彼女は深い眠りへと滑り込んでいった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah saw Kate entering the tent."
msgstr "サラはケイトがテントに入ってくるのを見た。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The moment their eyes met, Kate had a wide grin on her face."
msgstr "二人の視線が交差した瞬間、ケイトの顔には満面の笑みが浮かんだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I see I get here just in time."
msgstr "間に合ったみたいね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Funny."
msgstr "おかしいわね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Hey, I won't pass up on a show."
msgstr "ねえ、見世物なら見逃すわけないでしょ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Kate gestured at Sarah's body."
msgstr "ケイトはサラの体を指さした。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Is that any way to speak to your future Queen?"
msgstr "未来の女王である私にそんな口の利き方をするものですか？"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Oh no, my vile tongue has besmirched her Grace's honour."
msgstr "ああ、なんてことだ。この卑劣な舌で、彼女の殿下の尊厳を汚してしまった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Maybe my tongue can make it up?"
msgstr "私の言葉で埋め合わせができるかしら？"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Why are you here?"
msgstr "どうしてここにいるの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Just thought I'd check in with you after today. After the battle, I mean."
msgstr "今日、特に戦いの後、あなたの様子を確認しようと思って来たの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "You're strategy worked pretty well."
msgstr "あなたの戦略は、かなりうまく機能したようですね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I'm glad I made the right decision to send in the knights."
msgstr "騎士たちを投入した決断が正しかったと嬉しいわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I hear the entire field was red by the time they were done with those Tribesmen."
msgstr "戦いが終わった頃には、戦場全体が血で真っ赤になっていたと聞いたわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Not quite so gruesome. But yeah, you could see the aftermath."
msgstr "それほど凄惨というわけでもないわ。でも、ええ、その後の惨状は見て取れたわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I heard it was a bloodbath."
msgstr "血の海だったと聞いたわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Yeah, I underestimated the mobility of the Tribesmen archers."
msgstr "ええ、部族の弓兵たちの機動性を甘く見ていたわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I won't make that mistake again."
msgstr "もう同じ過ちは繰り返さないわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Don't beat yourself up about it. It's one battle, it won't make or break this war."
msgstr "自分を責めないで。これはただの一戦よ。これで戦争の成否が決まるわけじゃない。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She hoped it was true."
msgstr "彼女はそれが真実であることを願った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Fuck...on the rear I'm missing out on all the action."
msgstr "くそっ…後方にいるせいで、面白いところを全部見逃してるじゃないか。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You're upset you didn't get to fight?"
msgstr "戦えなかったことで落ち込んでるの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "A little."
msgstr "少しね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Most people here just pray they'll make it through this campaign alive."
msgstr "ここのほとんどの人間は、このキャンペーンを生き延びることさえ祈っているだけだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Yeah, well, most people wanna get old and have a million babies. I think I'll pass on both."
msgstr "ええ、まあ、ほとんどの人は年を取って、子供を何百万人も欲しいと思ってるでしょうね。私はその両方とも、パスするつもりだけど。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You might just surprise yourself."
msgstr "自分でも驚くかもしれないわよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "With babies?"
msgstr "子供がいるってこと？"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "No, I mean you might just happen to grow old."
msgstr "いや、つまり、たまたま年を取るかもしれないってことよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I'll be honest with you, I planned my life out a dozen ways, ain't any of them ending up with me as an old crone."
msgstr "正直に言うけど、私は人生を十数通りの方法で計画してきたわ。でも、そのどれもが、私が老婆になる結末には繋がってないの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You're not that eager to die, are you?"
msgstr "そんなに死にたくないんでしょ？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Kate looked down and shook her head."
msgstr "ケイトは下を見つめ、首を横に振った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "No...it's not like that either. It's just that I never thought I'd get to be all that old."
msgstr "いや…それもそうじゃないの。ただ、自分がそんなに年を取るなんて、考えたこともなかったってだけ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "A mercenary...well, you're lucky to get to forty."
msgstr "傭兵なんて…まあ、四十歳まで生きられたら幸運な方だよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The smart mercenaries took a few contracts and left. The stupid ones died."
msgstr "賢い傭兵は数件の契約をこなして去っていった。愚かな者たちは死んだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was a rare few that managed to survive decade after decade and still soldier on."
msgstr "数十年も生き残り、なおも戦い続ける者は、ごく稀だった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Maybe you won't have to be a mercenary anymore. When this is over."
msgstr "もう傭兵でいる必要はなくなるかもしれないわ。これが終わったら。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Maybe you can take on your old job, be a maid in my castle."
msgstr "もう、昔の仕事に戻って、私の城でメイドになることもできるかもしれないわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Fuck you too."
msgstr "お前もな。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Sure, maybe not that...but the country will be a mess, even if we win."
msgstr "ええ、それは違うかもしれないけど…たとえ私たちが勝ったとしても、国はめちゃくちゃになるでしょう。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I'll need someone like you. Someone close that I can trust."
msgstr "あなたのような人が必要なの。信頼できる、身近な人が。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "A knight."
msgstr "騎士よ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Kate suddenly looked up at her. Sarah imagined she saw surprise on her face."
msgstr "ケイトは突然彼女を見上げた。サラは、彼女の顔に驚きの色が浮かんだように感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Knighthood?"
msgstr "騎士になること？"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That's...for nobles."
msgstr "それは…貴族のためのものよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Sure, but special exemptions have been made in history before."
msgstr "ええ、でも歴史上、特別な例外が認められたこともありましたよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "And when I'm Queen, I can make you a Knight."
msgstr "そして私が女王になったら、あなたを騎士にすることができるわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah saw on Kate's face that she had never given the option any consideration."
msgstr "サラはケイトの顔から、彼女がその選択肢を全く考慮していなかったことを見抜いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I..."
msgstr "…考えさせてください。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I'll have to think about that."
msgstr "それについては考えさせてもらうわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But could I ask...why hestitate?"
msgstr "でも、聞かせてもらえるかな…なぜためらうの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Kate looked around the tent for a while, pausing as she considered her thoughts."
msgstr "ケイトはテントの中をしばらく見回し、考えを巡らせながら立ち止まった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "It's..."
msgstr "それは…"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I don't know. It feels weird to be back here."
msgstr "わからない。ここに戻ってきたって、なんだか変な感じがするの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You mean Rosanna?"
msgstr "ローズアンナのこと？"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I spend my life running away from it, and now I've walked back into it."
msgstr "私は一生、ここから逃げ続けてきたのに、今になってまたここに戻ってきてしまったのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I thought this place meant nothing to me, but now that I'm seeing the fields again...the memories of growing up here..."
msgstr "この場所は自分にとって何の意味もないと思っていたのに、今、再びこの野原を目の当たりにして…ここで育った記憶が蘇ってくるの…"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I'm afraid..."
msgstr "怖いの…"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I thought you weren't afraid of anything."
msgstr "あなたは何も怖くないと思っていたのに。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I'm not...at least, not when it comes to a good fight."
msgstr "私は…少なくとも、良い戦いに関しては怖くないわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "But it's more the idea of putting down roots here again..."
msgstr "でも、またここで根を下ろすっていう考えが、どうもね…"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "I feel like if I take that Knighthood...that's it, I'll be back here again. Stuck in Rosanna, despite everything."
msgstr "もしあの騎士の称号を受け入れたら…それで終わりよ。結局またここに戻ってくることになる。すべてにもかかわらず、ロザンナに縛られることになるの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I get it...but what else will you do? Leave after I take back my crown?"
msgstr "分かってる…でも、他に何ができるっていうの？私が王冠を取り戻したら、あなたは去ってしまうの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "That's the other part of it...I don't know what I'd do if I didn't stay..."
msgstr "それこそがもう一つの理由なの…もしここに残らなかったら、自分がどうなるか分からないの…"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "If I stay, I might regret it. If I leave, I might regret. Either which way..."
msgstr "もしここに残れば、後悔するかもしれない。もし去れば、それもまた後悔するかもしれない。どちらにしろ…"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked over and placed her hand on Kate's shoulder."
msgstr "サラは歩み寄り、ケイトの肩に手を置いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Think of it like this."
msgstr "そう考えてみて。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "If you stay and you regret it, at least you can cry on my shoulder every day."
msgstr "もし君が残って後悔したとしても、少なくとも毎日私の肩で泣けるだろうから。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Well, there's a compelling argument."
msgstr "まあ、それは説得力のある言い分だね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah saw Kate's eyes run across her body."
msgstr "サラはケイトの視線が自分の体をなめるように動くのを見た。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "And a pretty nice pair of shoulders too."
msgstr "それに、かなり心地よい肩でもあるわ。"

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Let Kate Stay"
msgstr "Kate を残す"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Just the shoulders?"
msgstr "肩だけ？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah felt Kate's mailed hands wrap around her waist, pulling her in closer."
msgstr "サラはケイトの鎧で覆われた手が自分の腰を包み込み、より近くに引き寄せるのを感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "You're such a tease."
