msgid "Nine times he brought her to climax before her body began to give out."
msgstr "九回も彼が彼女を絶頂に導いた後、ようやく彼女の体は限界を迎え始めた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Laying on the cold stone floor of the library, Sarah found her mind ever willing, but her body was ruined."
msgstr "図書館の冷たい石の床に横たわりながら、サラは心の中ではまだ彼への欲望に満ちていたが、体は完全に壊れてしまっていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "As the pleasure pulled back and the reality of her condition came back to her, Sarah could feel the real world intrude on her again."
msgstr "快楽が引き、自身の体の状態が現実として意識に戻ってくると、サラは再び現実世界が自分を侵してくるのを感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The pain across her body."
msgstr "彼女の体中に広がる痛み。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The cold stone."
msgstr "冷たい石。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She shivered."
msgstr "彼女は身震いした。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah could feel the spirit descend on her, but now sated it was not in lust but only in comfort."
msgstr "サラは霊が自分の上に降りてくるのを感じていたが、今やそれは欲望ではなく、ただの安らぎに満ちていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "There, rest. You are spend."
msgstr "ほら、休んで。もう疲れ果てたんだろ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah began to sob at the kindness of his warmth across her body, the spirit's best imitation of a hug."
msgstr "サラは彼の温もりが体全体に広がる優しさに、そしてその霊が抱擁を真似てくれたことに涙を流し始めた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She had not the energy to speak words, nor the mind to formulate any."
msgstr "彼女は言葉を発する気力も、思考をまとめる力も残っていなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Broken, exhausted and sobbing, Sarah slowly felt herself fade into sleep as she remained in the spirit's embrace."
msgstr "壊れ、疲れ果て、泣きじゃくるサラは、彼の温もりが体中に広がる中、精霊の抱擁の中でゆっくりと眠りに落ちていった。それは精霊が抱擁を模した最も優しき形だった。彼女には言葉を発する気力もなく、思考をまとめる余裕もなかった。"

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Rebuke the spirit"
msgstr "精霊を非難する"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I need to go, it's too late already."
msgstr "行かなきゃ。もう遅すぎるの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Together, the two of them returned back to the house."
msgstr "二人は一緒に家へと戻った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "By the time they returned, the night had already set in and Sarah retired to bed."
msgstr "二人が家に戻った頃には、すでに夜が更けており、サラは寝室へと退いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It had been weeks since Sarah first visited the library."
msgstr "サラが初めて図書館を訪れてから、すでに数週間が経過していた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Ever since, her days had been possessed by a single focus. Studying."
msgstr "それ以来、彼女の毎日はただ一つの目的、すなわち勉強に占められるようになった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Razaphel, a constant, provided her a seemingly endless list of books to read."
msgstr "ラザフェルは、変わることなく、彼女に読み続けるべき本のリストを、まるで尽きることがないかのように提供していた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "One subject more obscure than the next."
msgstr "次から次へと出てくる主題は、どれもこれもさらに難解なものばかりだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Ancient history texts on nations that Sarah had never even heard of."
msgstr "サラが聞いたこともない国々に関する古代史のテキスト。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Primary Alchemical instruction manuals."
msgstr "一次の錬金術指導マニュアル。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Even century old papers on the biology of obscure plant species."
msgstr "希少な植物種の生物学に関する百年前の論文でさえも。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "And Sarah read. She read everything he offered up to her, devouring the works."
msgstr "そしてサラは読んだ。彼が彼女に提供したものはすべて読み、その著作を貪るように読み込んだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps there was a pattern to the chaos, but she had not yet managed to resolve it."
msgstr "おそらく、この混乱の中にも何らかの法則があったのだろうが、彼女はまだそれを解明できていなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sitting behind the desk, Sarah watched as the spirit manifested itself into the room again."
msgstr "机の後ろに座りながら、サラは霊が再び部屋に姿を現すのを見ていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "In its hand, a copy of a new book. One more for the pile."
msgstr "その手には、外来植物の成長パターンに関する新しい本の写しが握られていた。山にまた一冊加わった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "This is a book on non-native flora growth patterns."
msgstr "これは外来植物の成長パターンに関する本だ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah sighed, exhausted as she threw her current book down on the desk."
msgstr "サラはため息をつき、疲れ果てた様子で今読んでいる本を机に投げつけた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Are you ever going to explain why I have to read all this?"
msgstr "いつになったら、なぜ私がこれらすべてを読まなければならないのか説明してくれるの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "You know why. If you want to understand their order, you must broaden the context of your understanding."
msgstr "理由は分かっているだろう。彼らの秩序を理解したいのなら、理解の文脈を広げなければならない。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah lifted up the tome that Razaphel had deposited."
msgstr "サラはラザフェルが置いた分厚い書物を手に取った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "And a book on plants is going to do that?"
msgstr "植物に関する本で、そんなことができるっていうの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The spirit paused for a moment."
msgstr "その霊はしばし言葉を止めた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "I understand that you are frustrated."
msgstr "君が苛立っているのは理解できる。"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Will you trust me that in time, very soon, I can explain everything to you?"
msgstr "時間が経てば、それもすぐに、すべてを説明できるということを信じてくれるだろうか？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah looked at the spirit. It's face-mask revealed nothing of its emotions. Its voice never wavered."
msgstr "サラは霊を見つめた。その顔の仮面からは感情が一切読み取れず、声も微塵も揺るがなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "How could one ever deduce if such a creature lied or spoke the truth."
msgstr "では、そのような生き物が嘘をついているのか、真実を語っているのか、どうやって見分けることなどできようか。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Then again, Sarah knew she had very few friends left that could help her with subjects of magic."
msgstr "しかし、サラは魔法の事柄で助けてくれる友人がほとんど残っていないことを知っていた。"

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Say you trust the spirit"
msgstr "精霊を信じる"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Yes...I trust you."
msgstr "ええ…あなたを信じています。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But even I have my limits, Razaphel."
msgstr "でも、私にも限界はあるのよ、ラザフェル。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "In time, you will have to bring me answers instead of books."
msgstr "いずれ、本ではなく答えを私に持ってくる時が来るわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "That time will come."
msgstr "その時が来ます。"

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Say you don't trust the spirit"
msgstr "「精霊を信じていない」と言う"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "No, I don't trust you."
msgstr "いいえ、あなたを信じていません。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You've given me no reason to do so. All you've given me is an endless supply of books."
msgstr "そんな理由を私に与えてくれたわけじゃない。あなたが私に与えたのは、尽きることのない本の山だけだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Books that leap from topic to topic like the list was drafted by a madman."
msgstr "本の内容が、まるで狂人がリストを作成したかのように、脈絡なく飛び交っている。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Who knows, maybe you are mad and I'm just wasting my time."
msgstr "さあね。もしかしたら、あなたが狂っていて、私がただ時間を無駄にしているだけかもしれないわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The spirit spun in the air."
msgstr "霊が空中で舞っていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "I promise that I will earn you trust, but only in due time, Sarah."
msgstr "サラ、いずれは君の信頼を得られると約束する。だが、それは適切な時が来たらだけだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "The answers will come. One day we shall speak truthfully."
msgstr "答えは必ずやってくる。いつか、我々は真実を語り合うことになるだろう。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "With that, the spirit vanished."
msgstr "そう言うと、その霊は消え去った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Staring at the book that remained, and the massive tome that had just been added to her list of work to do, Sarah sighed."
msgstr "残された本と、たった今自分のやるべき仕事リストに加わった分厚い大著をじっと見つめながら、サラはため息をついた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Falling back into her chair, she looked at the ceiling."
msgstr "椅子に深くもたれかかり、彼女は天井を見つめた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "In only a moment, she realized that whatever work remained, would have to be done another day. She was done, her brain more than exhausted."
msgstr "ほんのわずかな時間で、彼女は残りの作業がいつかまた行わなければならないことに気づいた。もう終わりだ。彼女の脳は完全に疲れ果てていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "No sooner had Sarah thought the thought, than she heard the creaking of the floorboards."
msgstr "サラがそう考えた途端、床板が軋む音が聞こえてきた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Sarah!!!"
msgstr "サラ！！！"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra's animated voice seemed to lighten up the room."
msgstr "サマヤラの生き生きとした声が部屋を明るくしたようだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah smiled at Samayra as she entered the room."
msgstr "サラは部屋に入ってきたサマヤラに微笑みかけた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "What is it Samayra?"
msgstr "どうしたの、サマヤラ？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra walked up towards the desk and planted her palms on the surface, leaning forward."
msgstr "サマヤラは机の方へ歩み寄り、両手をその表面に置いて身を乗り出した。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "For a moment, she looked deadly serious. Gathering her words."
msgstr "一瞬、彼女は恐ろしく真剣な表情を浮かべた。言葉を整理しながら。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "I'm bored."
msgstr "退屈してるの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You have a whole magical house, and you're bored?"
msgstr "魔法の家全体があるのに、退屈しているの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra rolled her eyes."
msgstr "サマヤラは目を回した。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Only so often that I can go to the bathhouse."
msgstr "私が風呂場に行けるのは、たまにだけなんだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "And unlike you, I can't spend all day reading."
msgstr "あなたとは違い、私は一日中本を読むわけにはいかないのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah swiftly poked Samayra, causing her to leap back, startled."
msgstr "サラはサマヤラを素早く突いて、彼女を驚かせて飛び上がらせた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Maybe it would do you some good, filling up that head with something other than love stories."
msgstr "それなら、その頭を恋愛小説以外のことで満たすのも、あなたには良いことかもしれないわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra scowled at her, but Sarah struggled to ever take the girl's anger very seriously."
msgstr "サマヤラは彼女を睨みつけたが、サラはその少女の怒りを真に受けることはほとんどなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well, I spend all my life in a palace, locked up. I don't want to be locked up here, reading more books!"
msgstr "ええ、私は一生を宮殿に閉じ込められて過ごしてきたのよ。ここでも閉じ込められて、本ばかり読み続けたくないわ！"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "I'm going to go out."
msgstr "外に出るわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah leapt up from her chair."
msgstr "サラは椅子から飛び立った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Samayra, you can't go out alone. Lethram is not...it's not a safe city."
msgstr "サマヤラ、一人で外に出ちゃだめよ。レトラムは…安全な街じゃないのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "There are parts of this city that are really dangerous, and if you don't know what parts to avoid..."
msgstr "この街には本当に危険な場所があるのよ。もしどの場所を避ければいいか知らなかったら…"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well, I guess in that case I'll need a guide."
msgstr "まあ、それなら案内人が必要になりそうね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra stuck out her tongue at Sarah."
msgstr "サマヤラはサラに舌を出した。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Still, are you going to let me walk out there all by myself?"
msgstr "それでも、私を一人でそこへ行かせるつもり？"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "No. I'll come with you."
msgstr "ううん。私も一緒に行くわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "To be honest, I was kind of looking for a distraction anyway."
msgstr "正直なところ、どうせ気を紛らわす何かを探していたところだったの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra had a wide smile on her face."
msgstr "サマヤラの顔には大きな笑みが浮かんでいた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Great, then let's go!"
msgstr "よかった、じゃあ行きましょう！"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra had already rushed for the door before Sarah was well and ready."
msgstr "サマヤラはサラが準備を終える前に、すでにドアに向かって駆け出していた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Rushing out behind her, Sarah tried to keep up with Samayra's energy."
msgstr "サラはサマヤラの後ろを急いで追いかけ、彼女のエネルギーに追いつこうと必死だった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah let her eyes drift across the study room."
msgstr "サラは書斎の部屋に目を走らせた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was this house."
msgstr "この家だったのだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She needed a break."
msgstr "彼女には休息が必要だった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I have to get some fresh air."
msgstr "新鮮な空気を吸わなきゃ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She spoke the words to nobody, and received as much as a reply."
msgstr "彼女は誰にも向かってその言葉を口にしたが、返答はほとんどなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah walked to the door and stepped outside, leaving the house and all her work behind her."
msgstr "サラはドアまで歩いていき、家と仕事すべてを後にして外に出た。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Stepping out of the house, Sarah was struck by the sudden wave of external stimuli."
msgstr "家から出て、サラは突然押し寄せる外部からの刺激に圧倒された。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "By now it was early in the afternoon and the city of Lethram had long buzzed to life."
msgstr "今や午後の早い時間になっており、レスラムの街はとっくに活気づいていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Inside the house, there was a distance, everything felt muted when watching the city through the windows."
msgstr "家の中では、窓越しに街を眺めていると、すべてが遠く、物音もかすかに聞こえるようだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But outside, in the open, everything felt raw and real."
msgstr "しかし外では、開けた空間で、すべてが生々しく、リアルに感じられた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The noises. The rushing waves of people. The smells of a big city."
msgstr "物音。押し寄せる人波。大都市の匂い。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah felt uneasy for a moment, so exposed."
msgstr "サラは一瞬、不安を感じた。あまりにも無防備だったからだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "A part of her wanted to run back inside, but she also knew she could not live in that house forever."
msgstr "彼女の心の一部は部屋に逃げ戻りたがっていたが、同時に、この家で永遠に暮らすことなどできないと分かっていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah could see Samayra was standing out on the street."
msgstr "サラはサマヤラが通りに立っているのを見ていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The girl seemed amazed."
msgstr "少女は驚いているようだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah remembered herself when she had first come to Lethram. She had been no less impressed by the city."
msgstr "サラは自分が初めてレトラムに来た時のことを思い出していた。あの時、彼女もまたこの街に同じくらい感銘を受けていたのだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra had lived even more isolated than Sarah had when growing up, so it was no surprise that it impressed her."
msgstr "サマヤラはサラが育った時よりもさらに孤立して生きてきたため、この街に感銘を受けるのも当然だった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "I...wow, it's-, I can't!"
msgstr "私…わあ、これは…、私には無理！"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra stumbled over her own words as she tried to formulate a thought."
msgstr "サマヤラは言葉を詰まらせながら、考えをまとめようとしていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Let's go, I think there's a place somewhere nearby."
msgstr "行こう。近くにどこか場所があると思うの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah lead and Samayra dutifully followed, gazing in stunned amazement of all the sights."
msgstr "サラが先導し、サマヤラは忠実に後をついていった。目の前の光景の数々に、彼女は呆然と見入っていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah decided to force herself to start walking."
msgstr "サラは自分を無理やり歩き始めた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Motion. Keep moving. Make the body move before the mind has time to convince itself otherwise."
msgstr "動き続けろ。思考が現実を否定する前に、体を動かすんだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Walking through the streets of Lethram, Sarah followed the curving road."
msgstr "レスラムの街を歩きながら、サラは曲がりくねった道に沿って進んだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "All around her, people were rushing up and down, dragging carts, carrying crates."
msgstr "彼女の周りでは、人々が忙しなく行き交い、荷車を引き、木箱を運んでいた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Lethram was a busy city, and it was especially so during the day."
msgstr "レトラムは賑やかな街で、特に昼間はそうだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "So near to the market district, this was where most of the trade that came in through the harbor district was offloaded."
msgstr "市場地区にほど近いこの場所は、港地区から入ってくる交易品のほとんどが荷下ろしされる場所だった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The sea trade had made Lethram obscenely wealthy and had allowed it to maintain its independence as a city in a world dominated by larger nations."
msgstr "海上貿易によってレズラムは莫大な富を得て、より大きな国々が支配する世界の中で、都市としての独立を維持することができたのだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Walking here, it made her reflect on how little she had known when she first left Rosanna."
msgstr "ここを歩いていると、ロザンナを初めて離れた頃には自分がどれほど何も知らなかったかを、彼女は考えさせられた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Her homeland had been prosperous enough when she left, but it was nothing compared to this place."
msgstr "彼女の故郷は、彼女がここを離れた時には十分に繁栄していたが、この場所と比べれば何でもないものだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Walking through these streets, she couldn't help but realize that this was a place where things seemed to happen."
msgstr "これらの通りを歩いていると、彼女はここが物事が起こる場所であることに気づかずにはいられなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "A place of importance. A place that decided how the world moved."
msgstr "重要な場所。世界がどう動くかを決定づける場所。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "That energy had never been in the air back home. Her home was a place of tradition and routine."
msgstr "故郷では、そんなエネルギーは空気中に流れていたことなどなかった。彼女の故郷は、伝統と日常の繰り返しに満ちた場所だったのだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There were times she found herself missing the security of that routine. Then there were times where Sarah loved the dynamism of this city."
msgstr "時には、彼女はその日常の安心感を恋しく思うこともあった。また、サラがこの街のダイナミズムを愛する時もあった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "As had been often of late, Sarah found her heart torn."
msgstr "最近よくあることだったが、サラは心が引き裂かれるのを感じていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Off to the side, Sarah could see a small crowd of people, gathered near a storefront, haggling over prices."
msgstr "横目で、サラは小さな人だかりが見えた。店の前で、人々が値段を交渉している。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Would she have been happier, she wondered, if she'd never taken a step on this path to begin with?"
msgstr "もし最初からこの道を一歩も歩まなかったら、自分はもっと幸せだったのだろうか、と彼女は思った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps if she had just resigned herself to living a simpler life."
msgstr "おそらく、もし彼女がもっと単純な生活を送ることに甘んじていれば、そうだったかもしれない。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "But Sarah also knew it was too late for that. Too late for regrets."
msgstr "しかしサラは、もう手遅れだと分かっていた。後悔するには遅すぎるのだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah saw the sign for a cafe."
msgstr "サラはカフェの看板を見つけた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She pointed it out to Samayra."
msgstr "彼女はサマヤラにそれを指摘した。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Here, let's go to this one."
msgstr "ほら、ここに行ってみよう。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra nodded, following Sarah's lead."
msgstr "サマヤラは頷き、サラの行動に従った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "She decided to go inside."
msgstr "彼女は中に入ることに決めた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Inside of the cafe, there was a calm atmosphere."
msgstr "カフェの内部は、落ち着いた雰囲気が漂っていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "A few patrons were seated by their own tables, occupied in their own conversations"
msgstr "数人の客がそれぞれのテーブルに座り、自分たちの会話に夢中になっていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah sat down at one of the tables."
msgstr "サラはテーブルの片方に腰を下ろした。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra sat down opposite of her."
msgstr "サマヤラは彼女の向かいに座った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah smiled as she watched Samayra's wide eyes sliding across the room."
msgstr "サラは、サマヤラの大きく見開かれた目が部屋中をさまようのを見ながら微笑んだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Around them, waiters were rushing back and forth from the bar, taking and delivering orderse."
msgstr "二人の周りでは、ウェイターたちがバーと客の間を忙しく行き来し、注文を受けたり届けたりしていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "It's just like the palace back home in Bagrad, except...the servants have servants?"
msgstr "故郷のバグラードにある宮殿とそっくりだけど…ここには使用人にも使用人がいるの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "This city is a little more equal than where you or I came from."
msgstr "この街は、あなたや私が来た場所よりも、少しは平等だわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "People work, but even those that work make enough money to visit places like this."
msgstr "人々は働いているけれど、働いている人たちでさえ、ここのような場所を訪れるのに十分な稼ぎをしているのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra nodded as she listened to Sarah explain."
msgstr "サマヤラはサラの説明を聞きながら頷いた。この街は、彼女やサマヤラが来た場所よりも少しは平等だ。人々は働いているが、働いている者でさえ、このような場所を訪れるのに十分な金を稼いでいる。そして…ここにいる人々は誰も奴隷ではないのだろうか？"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "So...none of these people are slaves?"
msgstr "じゃあ…ここの人たちは誰も奴隷じゃないの？"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Slavery is strictly forbidden in Lethram."
msgstr "奴隷制度はレトラムでは厳しく禁じられているわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah could see Samayra process that fact."
msgstr "サラはサマヤラがその事実を消化していく様子を見て取れた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Huh, my father had always said that slaves were a natural part of the world. How empires were build."
msgstr "ええ、父はいつも、奴隷は世界の自然な一部だと言っていたわ。帝国がそうやって築かれたのだと。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "But this city is pretty big, and it doesn't have slaves at all..."
msgstr "でも、この街はかなり大きいのに、奴隷が一人もいないなんて…"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "If anything, it's likely Lethram has been wealthier than Bagrad for a good many centuries."
msgstr "むしろ、レトラムはバグラッドよりも何世紀にもわたってずっと裕福だった可能性が高い。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah saw Samayra's face suddenly turn sad."
msgstr "サラはサマヤラの顔が突然悲しみに変わったのを見た。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "I...never thought about it like that."
msgstr "私…そんな風に考えたことはなかったわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Bagrad. The palace. Up until recently they were the only places I've ever known."
msgstr "バグラド。宮殿。最近まで、私が知っていたのはそこだけだったの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah saw the girl go quiet for a moment, then she looked up."
msgstr "サラは、少女がしばし黙り込んだのを見て、それから彼女が顔を上げるのを見た。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Do you think I was a bad person for living in that palace?"
msgstr "私があの宮殿で暮らしていたことは、悪いことだったと思う？"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "For living with so much while others had so little?"
msgstr "たくさんのものを持って生きてきたのに、他の人たちはあんなに少ないものしか持っていなかったのよ、って？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah reached over and took Samayra's hand."
msgstr "サラは手を伸ばしてサマヤラの手を取った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I think that if you're even questioning these things, you're probably a lot better than most."
msgstr "あなたがそんなことを疑問に思っているだけでも、おそらく大半の人よりずっと良い人間なんだろうね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "And I think given where you were raised, you never had much of a chance to push back."
msgstr "それに、あなたが育った環境を考えれば、抵抗する機会なんてほとんどなかったはずだと思うの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Who knows, maybe if the world had played out differently, you might have inherited the throne and changed all of that."
msgstr "誰にも分からないわ。もし世界が違った形で進んでいたら、あなたは王位を継承して、そのすべてを変えていたかもしれないのよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra nodded, but still seemed uncertain."
msgstr "サマヤラは頷いたが、まだ確信が持てないようだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Maybe...I don't know."
msgstr "たぶん…わからないわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You think you would have kept slavery?"
msgstr "そう思うの？奴隷制度を維持していたと思う？"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Not that, but I think...I just never had to think about any of that."
msgstr "そういうわけじゃないけど、たぶん…私はそんなことについて考える必要が一度もなかったの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "I spend my life in the library. The gardens. I just had to do what my father told me."
msgstr "私は一生を図書館で過ごしてきた。庭園で。父の言う通りに生きるだけでよかったの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Now...I'm here, and I see all of this...it's a lot."
msgstr "今…ここに来て、このすべてを目の当たりにすると…本当にすごいことだわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I understand. I had a lot of the same feelings that you have when I first came here all those years ago."
msgstr "分かります。何年も前に私が初めてここに来た時、あなたと同じような感情をたくさん抱いたものです。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "All I had ever known was my homeland, the castle I had been raised in."
msgstr "私がこれまで知っていたのは、故郷と、私が育った城だけだった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "When that was all gone...I felt lost too for a long time."
msgstr "それがすべてなくなってしまった時…私も長い間、途方に暮れていたわ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was magic that gave me a way back to getting some degree of control over my life."
msgstr "それは魔法が、私の人生をある程度コントロールできる道を与えてくれたの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra smiled and nodded."
msgstr "サマヤラは微笑み、頷いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Maybe that's what I need. Some way to get some control back."
msgstr "たぶん、それが必要なんだろう。再び人生をある程度コントロールできる方法が。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Sure, but you're in no rush. You're safe in the house, in this city, with my protection."
msgstr "ええ、でも急ぐ必要はないわ。この家も、この街も安全よ。私が守ってあげるから。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You've been through a lot. The best thing for you now is to try and just recover."
msgstr "あなたはこれまで多くのことを経験してきたわ。今あなたにとって一番良いのは、ただ回復しようと努力することよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra eagerly nodded."
msgstr "サマヤラは熱心に頷いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "I think some food might help with that."
msgstr "食事でもしたら、その助けになると思うんだけど。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah laughed and raised her hand, calling over one of the waiters."
msgstr "サラは笑いながら手を挙げ、ウェイターの一人を呼び止めた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Each gave their order and not long after the food was delivered. Money formed no problem, Sarah kept finding piles of it stashed away in the house."
msgstr "それぞれが注文を終えると、ほどなくして食事が運ばれてきた。金の問題などなかった。サラは家の中に隠してあった金を次々と見つけていたからだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Huh...fish..."
msgstr "え…魚…"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Is that a problem?"
msgstr "問題ある？"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "No, we just didn't get a lot of that in Bagrad."
msgstr "いいえ、ただバグラドではそういうものがあまり手に入らなかっただけよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "We weren't very close to an ocean, and the merchants prefered to bring foods that could survive a trip through the desert."
msgstr "うん、魚が嫌いなら、この街は問題になるかもしれないね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Yeah, if you don't like fish, this city can be a problem."
msgstr "ええ、魚が好きじゃないなら、この街は問題になるかもね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Well I love fish."
msgstr "ええ、私は魚が大好きなの。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "With a growing hunger, each of them began to dig into their meal."
msgstr "空腹が増すにつれて、二人はそれぞれ食事に手を付け始めた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "As they ate their share, each swapped stories of their life from before they met."
msgstr "食事をしながら、二人は出会う前のそれぞれの人生について語り合った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It continued to surprise Sarah just how much she had in common with a girl who had been born on the other side of the world."
msgstr "サラは、世界の反対側で生まれた少女とこれほど多くの共通点があることに、驚き続けていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The isolation of the castle. The weight of nobility. All were things that few people could share, but this girl understood intuitively."
msgstr "城の孤立。貴族としての重圧。それらはほとんど人が共有できないものだったが、この少女は直感的に理解していた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Hey there ladies."
msgstr "やあ、お嬢さんたち。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "All of a sudden, Sarah heard a familiar voice calling out to the both of them."
msgstr "突然、サラは聞き慣れた声が二人を呼ぶのを耳にした。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "From the corner of her eyes, she saw a man stand up next to the table."
msgstr "視界の隅で、彼女はテーブルの隣に立つ男の姿を捉えた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Enjoying yourselves, I hope."
msgstr "楽しんでくれてるかな？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra looked at Alaric and smiled."
msgstr "サマヤラはアラリックを見て微笑んだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Very much so, the food here is great!"
msgstr "ええ、もちろんです。ここの食事は最高ですよ！"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Well I'm glad to hear that."
msgstr "それは聞いて嬉しいよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Alaric reached out with one hand, and Samayra reacted, grabbing and shaking his."
msgstr "アラリックが片手を伸ばすと、サマヤラはそれに応じ、彼の手を掴んで振った。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah lunged forward and pulled Samayra's hand back."
msgstr "サラは飛びかかり、サマヤラの手を引いて引き戻した。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Don't shake his hand."
msgstr "彼の手を振るな。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Samayra seemed shocked and confused."
msgstr "サマヤラは驚きと混乱を隠せない様子だった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Why not? Who is he?"
msgstr "なぜダメなの？彼は誰？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Alaric continued to smile."
msgstr "アラリックは微笑みを続けた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Me? Ooh me and Sarah here are good friends, aren't we, Sarah?"
msgstr "私？おや、私とサラは仲の良い友人でしょう、サラ？"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I'm sure you have somewhere else to be. Maybe some old lady dropped her wallet nearby?"
msgstr "きっと他に予定があるんだろう？もしかして、近くにどこかの老婆が財布を落としたとか？"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Always funny running into you Sarah."
msgstr "いつも通り、君に会うのは面白いね、サラ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "And who knew you had such a lovely friend?"
msgstr "そして、君にこんなに素敵な友人がいたなんて、誰が知っていたんだろう？"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "But no, I actually don't have anywhere I need to be right now."
msgstr "でも、いや、実は今行くべき場所なんてないんだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah stood up from the table."
msgstr "サラはテーブルから立ち上がった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Samayra, stay here."
msgstr "サマヤラ、ここに残って。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah grabbed Alaric by his shirt and began to drag him outside of the cafe."
msgstr "サラはアラリックのシャツを掴み、彼をカフェの外へ引きずり始めた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Outside, the sun was already setting and the streets had grown significantly quieter."
msgstr "外ではすでに日が沈み、通りはずいぶんと静かになっていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah continued to drag Alaric, off to the side of the cafe, away from anyone else."
msgstr "サラはアラリックを引きずり続け、カフェの脇、他の人から離れた場所へと向かった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Finally, far enough from prying eyes, Sarah released Alaric and turned to face him."
msgstr "ようやく、人目から十分に離れたところで、サラはアラリックを解放し、彼の方を向いた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You have a lot of fucking nerve coming over to me like that."
msgstr "よくもそんな顔で私に近づいてこられたわね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "As always, his face was painted with that casual and arrogant smile of his."
msgstr "いつものように、彼の顔にはあの無頓着で傲慢な笑みが浮かんでいた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "I just thought it was funny running into you, and I saw your little girlfriend over there, quite a stunner, so I just thought-"
msgstr "君にこんな風に会えて、なんだか面白かったんだ。それに、あそこにいる君の彼女も見たけど、かなり魅力的じゃないか。だから、ちょっと…"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Well don't."
msgstr "やめて。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Don't think, don't talk, don't do shit to cause trouble, do you understand?"
msgstr "考えるな、話すな、面倒を起こすようなことは一切するな、分かった？"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Or what?"
msgstr "そうじゃないのか！"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You know or what!"
msgstr "分かってるの？！"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah felt the heat of magical fire rising from around her hands. She could turn him to ash as easily as the snap of her finger."
msgstr "サラは魔法の炎の熱が手の周りから立ち上るのを感じた。彼女は指を鳴らすだけで彼を灰に変えることができるのだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Aah, yes, you're going to set me on fire, I remember."
msgstr "ああ、そうか、俺を燃やすつもりなんだな。覚えてるよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "He didn't seem all the impressed."
msgstr "彼はさほど感心しているようには見えなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "But you see, there's a little problem that you've forgotten."
msgstr "ほら、君が忘れてしまっている小さな問題があるんだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "You see, there are actually laws in Lethram."
msgstr "ほら、レスラムにはちゃんと法律があるんだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Even for mages."
msgstr "魔法使いでさえもね。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "So while you might have been in your right to kill me back at your house, cause I'll admit I was up to no good, out here..."
msgstr "だから、君の家で僕を殺す権利があったかもしれないけど、認めるよ、僕もろくなことしてなかった。でも、ここでは…"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Well everyone has seen I didn't do nothin but talk to a few pretty girls."
msgstr "まあ、みんな見たでしょう？俺は綺麗な女の子たちと話す以外、何もしてないって。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "And that hardly deserves the death penalty."
msgstr "それに、そんなことで死刑に処されるなんて、到底あり得ないだろう。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah gritted her teeth, a rage growing inside of her."
msgstr "サラは歯を食いしばり、怒りが内側で燃え上がっていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There was nothing more she wanted than to set this bastard on fire, but she also knew he was right. There were laws."
msgstr "彼女が最も望んでいたのは、このクズを焼き殺すことだったが、彼が正しいことも分かっていた。法律があるのだ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Just stay away!"
msgstr "離れていて！"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "No."
msgstr "いいえ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "His answer was swift and definitive."
msgstr "彼の返答は迅速かつ断固としていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "No law in the world that says I can't wander on in back to that cafe and sit down with you two lovely ladies and chat."
msgstr "世の中に、俺があのカフェに戻って、お前たち二人の可愛い女性たちと一緒に座って話してはいけないなんて法律なんてないだろう。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Maybe I'll tell her all about what great lay you are."
msgstr "もしかしたら、君がどれほど素晴らしい相手か、彼女に全部話してやるかもしれないな。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Who knows, maybe I'll even take her for a spin-"
msgstr "誰にも分からない。もしかしたら、彼女を連れてドライブにでも行ってみるかもしれない。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah stabbed her finger into his chest."
msgstr "警告するわ。そんなこと考えもしないで。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I'm warning you. Don't even think about it."
msgstr "警告するわ。そんなこと、考えることさえもよさないで。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "What are you going to do about it?"
msgstr "それで、どうするつもりなんだ？"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah stumbled over the words."
msgstr "サラは言葉に詰まった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I...well...I...."
msgstr "わ…あの…わ…"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "There wasn't much of anything that she could do."
msgstr "彼女にできることなど、ほとんど何もなかった。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "But tell you what, how about you scratch my back and I'll scratch yours."
msgstr "でもな、どうだ？お前が俺の背中を掻いてくれたら、俺もお前の背中を掻いてやるよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah looked him in the eyes."
msgstr "サラは彼の目を見つめた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Well, when I'm talkin about my back, I'm of course talkin about my dick."
msgstr "まあ、俺の背中って話だけどな、もちろん俺のチンコのことだよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "See, I got a ragin hard on and not much of anyone that can take care of it."
msgstr "ほらな、俺はめちゃくちゃ硬くなっちまってるんだが、それを片付けてくれる奴がほとんどいないんだよ。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah felt how Alaric suddenly grabbed her hand and pushed it up against his crotch."
msgstr "サラは、アラリックが突然彼女の手を掴み、彼の股間に押し当てたのを感じた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Instinctively she pulled her hand back, but she had felt enough to know he wasn't lying."
msgstr "本能的に彼女は手を引いたが、彼が嘘をついていないことは十分に感じ取っていた。"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Easy. You take care of me, here in this alley, and I'll leave you and your friend alone. Simple."
msgstr "簡単だ。この路地裏で俺の世話をすれば、お前と友達には手を出さない。単純な話だ。"

